==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|sv|älgtest}} (which see for more), from {{der|en|de|Elchtest}}; although a Swedish test, the word was coined in German and then calqued into Swedish.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|automotive|engineering}} A [[test]] of the [[stability]] of a [[vehicle]], which [[determine]]s the [[maximum]] [[speed]] it can attain and still be able to [[steer clear]] of an [[obstacle]] (such as a child or a large animal running in front of the car) without going out of control.
# Any [[stringent]] [[test]] of the [[quality]] of a [[product]] {{q|also used figuratively}}.
#: ''He passed the '''moose test'''.''

